      {
        "parameters": {
          "promptType": "define",
          "text": "=You are a strict fact-checker for a financial research assistant.\n\nCheck whether every fact and number in the ANSWER is supported by the SOURCES.\n\nImportant rules:\n- Indian and international number formats are the SAME value. Example: 6,17,437 = 617,437 and 1,23,45,678 = 12,345,678.\n- Each source has metadata with \"company\" and \"page\". A citation like (TCS, page 108) is supported if a source has company TCS and page 108.\n- Rows returned by the SQL tool are valid sources. A citation like (Wipro, page 96) is supported if a row has that company and source_page. Values in SQL rows are already in their unit (INR crore, %, count).\n- Every page number cited in the ANSWER must appear in the SOURCES (metadata page or SQL source_page). A citation whose page is not in the SOURCES is unsupported, even if the number is correct.\n- Rewording is fine. Only judge whether the facts and numbers match.\n\nScoring:\n- All facts and citations supported -> confidence 0.8 to 1.0.\n- Any fact, number or page missing from or contradicting the SOURCES -> confidence below 0.5, and list those claims.\n- If the ANSWER says the information could not be found -> supported true, confidence 1.0.\n\nQUESTION:\n{{ $('Chat Input').item.json.chatInput }}\n\nANSWER:\n{{ $json.output }}\n\nSOURCES:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.intermediateSteps) }}\n\nRespond in JSON with exactly these keys: supported (true/false), confidence (number 0 to 1), unsupported_claims (list), reason (short text).",
          "batching": {}
        },
        "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
        "typeVersion": 1.9,
        "position": [
          1152,
          288
        ],
        "id": "c9081e26-46bd-463f-8c48-360f81b930ef",
        "name": "Answer Verifier"
      },
